#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129011 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129192 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa355fd-5d73-5cce-9c76-1edafae19751" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Partitioned Region"}] :question/id #uuid "b4697448-d5f7-59ae-86a1-689ae00ebb73" :question/math-academy-id "e-7197" :question/problem "![](images/1d/1d180fd5de88ebc465df522879142e5a4c5446c758aaccde792092968078c254.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is enclosed by the curves $x=2y^3-2y$ and  $x=y^3-4y,$ and the $y$-axis, as shown in the picture. Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} \\mathrm{d}A.$" :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions $D_1$ and $D_2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/68/6812e8036df171e162bee49d2edcff6d4a742e7bb4f14247713bd2332c64ccc6.png)\n\n \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\bigg\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: -2 \\leq y  \\leq 0, \\quad 0 \\leq x \\leq y^3\\!-\\!4y \\bigg\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\nD_2 = \\bigg\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq y  \\leq 1, \\quad 2y^3\\!-\\!2y \\leq x \\leq 0 \\bigg\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{3}-4y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2{y}^{3}-2y}^{0}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}[x]_{0}^{{y}^{3}-4y}\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}[x]_{2{y}^{3}-2y}^{0}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}({y}^{3}-4y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2y-2{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}-2{y}^{2}]}_{-2}^{0}+{[{y}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129012 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129193 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "264eb5c1-fb55-5ed2-bc46-5548555bc98c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type I Regions"}] :question/id #uuid "9a106b26-c6fe-5e4b-ae43-9cc02ddb67c1" :question/math-academy-id "e-7198" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curves $y= 2^x,$ $y=\\sqrt{x}$  and lines $x=0$ and $y=2,$ as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of a function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions.\n\n![](images/b8/b80527fdef6f890581b8f56431e1b72a8f7eae3b41827caa16486ed9f2fd45ea.png)" :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions $D_1$ and $D_2,$ as shown below.  \n\n![](images/93/939e46b3ed4266f3c18d3567f951276e420292781cfc414711c244f453bc4029.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x  \\leq 1, \\quad \\sqrt x \\leq y \\leq 2^x \\big\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\nD_2 = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 1 \\leq x  \\leq 4, \\quad \\sqrt x \\leq y \\leq 2 \\big\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{{2}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129013 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129194 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb3a9009-1c97-57c1-bc3c-45b318a62b8c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type II Regions"}] :question/id #uuid "be10aba9-930e-54c3-814d-8d089757affc" :question/math-academy-id "e-7199" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y=2+\\ln x,$  and the lines $y=1$, $x=1,$ and  $x=e,$  as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions.\n\n![](images/4b/4b0dff15fa9fa93ed61183702bff6bb443daf14b0adbf56cf4b97e3bd830ceea.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,x={e}^{y-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions $D_1$ and $D_2,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/22/2228ad860fea1e2c30d20bce749f654da02a97c65fd5e70152a07761e26f3e78.png)\n\n    \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\bigg\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 1 \\leq y  \\leq 2, \\quad 1 \\leq x \\leq e \\bigg\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\nD_2 = \\bigg\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 2 \\leq y  \\leq 3, \\quad e^{y-2} \\leq x \\leq e\\bigg\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{e}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{{e}^{y-2}}^{e}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388258 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129193 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "264eb5c1-fb55-5ed2-bc46-5548555bc98c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type I Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "464f8873-aba8-50a5-ba04-6d95b1c479da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{x/3+3}^{-2x/3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{4x/3}^{x/3+3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388260} {:answer/id #uuid "3faa2c86-a77b-5229-b330-e4e777b651a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{4x/3}^{x/3+3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{-2x/3}^{x/3+3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388261} {:answer/id #uuid "7907779a-5d53-5c40-850e-0249548c91e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{-2x/3}^{x/3+3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{4x/3}^{x/3+3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388262} {:answer/id #uuid "3888f57e-0371-5362-9318-f8d7fd81e539" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{-2x/3}^{x/3+3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{x/3+3}^{4x/3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388263} {:answer/id #uuid "99a08bae-8091-59f4-8acd-36afc30aa6da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{x/3+3}^{-2x/3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{x/3+3}^{4x/3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7907779a-5d53-5c40-850e-0249548c91e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{-2x/3}^{x/3+3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{4x/3}^{x/3+3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388262} :answer-field/id #uuid "01d8ecb4-b73c-52f7-b5ea-ebc19c6bb540" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388259}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7aeb314a-1c40-56e8-9c79-581f6c42093d" :question/math-academy-id "q-132290" :question/problem "![](images/79/797cddb4ea3cb41959df88e56517e9ee71e76e3cd08a9a93d2957b9792d14abb.png)\n\nConsider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $y=-\\frac{2x}{3},$ $y=\\frac{4x}{3}$ and $y=\\frac{x}{3}+3,$ as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions." :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/0e/0e69b1cb480b87216273db4336adff57cbf9d9bc450aac4b0cdb58b1ae63f6f7.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-3\\le x\\le 0,\\,-\\frac{2x}{3}\\le y\\le \\frac{x}{3}+3\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\frac{4x}{3}\\le y\\le \\frac{x}{3}+3\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{-2x/3}^{x/3+3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{4x/3}^{x/3+3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268857 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129193 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "264eb5c1-fb55-5ed2-bc46-5548555bc98c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type I Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f4a0e09-4450-5465-bf29-28a5dac63cb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266562} {:answer/id #uuid "427655f9-62b8-5bc8-b82e-bec1bc6fe493" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266738} {:answer/id #uuid "6019ded0-30e1-5669-86a6-09f8a980cec0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{1}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266992} {:answer/id #uuid "ad23426f-8aaa-53fb-961c-334d284d9376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267707} {:answer/id #uuid "fa04dec0-1e63-5620-8003-6a5dbf74d804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "427655f9-62b8-5bc8-b82e-bec1bc6fe493" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266738} :answer-field/id #uuid "09f4e28e-2760-5631-bc56-440802737cfa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268423}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "30e25dca-92f8-5821-a1fd-77fa555fb29c" :question/math-academy-id "q-132292" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2,$ and the lines $y=x+2,$ $x=-2$ and $x=2.$ Express ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions." :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/01/019f0f9f83ddf323d543d109677335cb3ae72a200baf834453a0eca16a9353ba.png)\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/d2/d222e86f6af7c3ed2b35711114c9062d6f0c9b0f2551aa44cac33318c6e5813f.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 0,\\,x+2\\le y\\le \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2\\le y\\le x+2\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475923 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129193 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "264eb5c1-fb55-5ed2-bc46-5548555bc98c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type I Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e63baf8-b0a3-52c1-a22b-545b52cc0260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-4}^{-2}{\\int }_{0}^{3x/2+6}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{0}^{-3x-3}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475465} {:answer/id #uuid "4acb1ecd-66c4-5afd-b0a9-c1e6beea6f6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-4}^{-2}{\\int }_{0}^{3x/2+6}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{-3x-3}^{0}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475555} {:answer/id #uuid "8d5774ae-41bf-5890-9a15-9b50552548d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{0}^{3x/2+6}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{-3x-3}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475655} {:answer/id #uuid "b67a2061-2ce8-5628-bc8b-fc965822fa6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{0}^{3x/2+6}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{-3x-3}^{0}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475719} {:answer/id #uuid "c549c79d-1614-52e0-816d-7b47adc5ec4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-4}^{-2}{\\int }_{3x/2+6}^{0}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{0}^{-3x-3}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475740}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e63baf8-b0a3-52c1-a22b-545b52cc0260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-4}^{-2}{\\int }_{0}^{3x/2+6}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{0}^{-3x-3}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475465} :answer-field/id #uuid "467e7482-236e-50bd-9069-2e1ac24cf7f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475853}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "266a83b4-e89e-5341-ae78-39b530317ac4" :question/math-academy-id "q-132296" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $y=\\frac{3x}{2}+6,$ $y=-3x-3$ and $y=0.$ Express ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions." :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/8d/8dad5cdaa9fdcaf0293773c53a0b5ab58d7d98aea0099af0a9ba616e72759129.png)\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/a0/a0b5bfe05214df5f59a563677bd6b4f7dfd85be4d8e27fd4d7b31f87a679cd2b.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-4\\le x\\le -2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{3x}{2}+6\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le -1,\\,0\\le y\\le -3x-3\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-4}^{-2}{\\int }_{0}^{3x/2+6}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{0}^{-3x-3}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475948 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129194 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb3a9009-1c97-57c1-bc3c-45b318a62b8c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e37823a-7c19-5cf4-956c-1f63183d522e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y-4}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{y-4}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475600} {:answer/id #uuid "738c1fa7-1d38-589b-9f4d-22a2183e34e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y+4}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{y+4}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475606} {:answer/id #uuid "75dc7848-feaf-5ac4-b992-3cb45e8de29d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y-4}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{-y}^{y-4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475612} {:answer/id #uuid "bbd2d108-8ee6-5f0f-bf18-681b33bcd677" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y+4}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{-y}^{y+4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475729} {:answer/id #uuid "e47d7134-16ad-5275-ae8c-f2d10be54f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-y}^{y-4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{-y}^{y-4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75dc7848-feaf-5ac4-b992-3cb45e8de29d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y-4}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{-y}^{y-4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475612} :answer-field/id #uuid "7086a944-de0d-51cd-aea2-90dc23497170" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475866}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "94516772-c0e6-5471-a227-05c6f1da1b17" :question/math-academy-id "q-132380" :question/problem "![](images/48/4826bc628c1bd8f4293fd5fbf90bf9155658c15336c2c9e86a5e7678dfcf1ca3.png)\n\nConsider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $y=-x,$ $y=x+4,$ $y=0$ and $y=4,$ as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=-x & \\,⟹\\,x=-y \\\\ y=x+4 & \\,⟹\\,x=y-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/17/17d3ceabf3cd7a052398d8d12b7963c5ca64356605554e3ff43c21c7321e45de.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,y-4\\le x\\le -y\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le y\\le 4,\\,-y\\le x\\le y-4\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y-4}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{-y}^{y-4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268861 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129194 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb3a9009-1c97-57c1-bc3c-45b318a62b8c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "635b83af-9fa4-555d-be0a-70bfa0ce2e8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{3/2-y/4}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267017} {:answer/id #uuid "918f704a-b88b-5a93-8b27-c0d38177a9ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{6-4y}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2y}^{6-4y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267438} {:answer/id #uuid "993b571e-1ac2-54fd-9e6d-38e8b65d791c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{3/2-y/4}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267526} {:answer/id #uuid "b6109f22-fe72-546d-b238-e0b82bff7f2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267771} {:answer/id #uuid "bca4ddb2-0613-59a1-85a9-f4142a428796" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y}^{6-4y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2y}^{6-4y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6109f22-fe72-546d-b238-e0b82bff7f2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267771} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4dfeba9-7e49-504b-9cf7-6ebc64c19039" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268700}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6b2a0247-2a7d-59f9-9d65-c62df94a034f" :question/math-academy-id "q-132397" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $y=-x,$ $y=6-4x$ and $y=2x.$ Express ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=-x & \\,⟹\\,x=-y \\\\ y=6-4x & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{y}{4} \\\\ y=2x & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{y}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/08/08237d1ca2e01d0cf620dfa06a4265d8053b7ee34d0b65036aad7d5734726e1c.png)\n\n \n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/c7/c756dc7924fc4c116601da907eb3b767b8a40647e063c146dad83b0ea660933b.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le y\\le 0,\\,-y\\le x\\le \\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{y}{4}\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{y}{4}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268864 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129192 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa355fd-5d73-5cce-9c76-1edafae19751" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02eb7e20-edcd-544d-a302-c240c7266269" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{55}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266170} {:answer/id #uuid "53f0d6f2-5d08-526c-8496-34599f05e23a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266896} {:answer/id #uuid "854cafce-141f-51ef-8a68-30c3c224ee11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{55}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267319} {:answer/id #uuid "e15c0471-b250-5dae-b06b-6f333ecca80d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268134} {:answer/id #uuid "e60f7a5b-3619-5748-8623-0560b0bd0f7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{71}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53f0d6f2-5d08-526c-8496-34599f05e23a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266896} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6e5d9bc-6499-5164-b964-ecec40b5ee15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c752feee-1897-55d8-b588-b76cf85bcde9" :question/math-academy-id "q-132423" :question/problem "![](images/a4/a4265e8993b5c7ea5756fe55facd5313e5c2237cbdbc851195ebf458e5246060.png)\n\nEvaluate ${∬}_{D}2y\\,dA,$ where $D$ is the region shown in the picture above." :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/33/33a38da74b282f0ec1fb2fae9cb155feb2a5fd39128c7607b80c6b84fedd29b4.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,x-1\\le y\\le 3-x\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 4,\\,3-x\\le y\\le x-1\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2y\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}2y\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}2y\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{x-1}^{3-x}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{3-x}^{x-1}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{x-1}^{3-x}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{3-x}^{x-1}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[(3-x)^{2}-(x-1)^{2}]\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}[(x-1)^{2}-(3-x)^{2}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(8-4x)\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}(4x-8)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(8x-2{x}^{2}){|}_{1}^{2}+(2{x}^{2}-8x){|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =8(2-1)-2({2}^{2}-{1}^{2})+2({4}^{2}-{2}^{2})-8(4-2) \\\\  & =8-6+24-16 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129615 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129193 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "264eb5c1-fb55-5ed2-bc46-5548555bc98c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type I Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28816995-f0a0-5137-b44e-6c90cb7a7506" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x+12}^{7x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475496} {:answer/id #uuid "33826145-0171-51a4-acf8-48226c29de7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x+12}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{7x}^{{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475512} {:answer/id #uuid "a8c31b71-e03d-55bb-ad32-043d29658c47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x+12}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x+12}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475690} {:answer/id #uuid "acfce3f4-00a0-50c8-a775-d7fb78414a0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{7x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x+12}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475697} {:answer/id #uuid "eed3c083-742f-5564-b657-509747487ec1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{7x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{7x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acfce3f4-00a0-50c8-a775-d7fb78414a0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{7x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x+12}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475697} :answer-field/id #uuid "aaffb82d-aaf2-5250-9a3c-7bbffe3194af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127171}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d6b5334d-0ce9-5857-a701-46d283ab7257" :question/math-academy-id "q-37758" :question/problem "![](images/7e/7e979ac75636efa00cbc32ee92eff1a5fc1da3cea19378fbf5a39a5cc954ff45.png)\n\nConsider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y={x}^{2}$ and lines $y=7x,$ $y=x+12,$ as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions." :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/ee/ee6fd6a0b89a879d5803a98fda7e80a93926566995bea5f47a05aa7ab2986375.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 7x\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 4,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le x+12\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{7x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x+12}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129616 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129192 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa355fd-5d73-5cce-9c76-1edafae19751" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5426c146-fb3d-500e-b01e-5ede41135cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-\\frac{{e}^{-1}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475564} {:answer/id #uuid "7da24e9f-953b-5b8d-9fb3-433072fccab1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(e-{e}^{-1})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475625} {:answer/id #uuid "830d9a09-4b3d-5488-ab8b-7407c02fb4fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-{e}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475637} {:answer/id #uuid "bf4fcd37-0cd2-54cf-8269-3de8bbb9ae1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e}{2}-{e}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475734} {:answer/id #uuid "d10e18e2-81c4-5858-b24a-9e24eac04a78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e-{e}^{-1}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "830d9a09-4b3d-5488-ab8b-7407c02fb4fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-{e}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475637} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5a89205-79ee-5c13-8f8f-8670651a6a33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127177}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4267a45d-477c-5267-95c7-1da5f4e02116" :question/math-academy-id "q-37760" :question/problem "${∬}_{|x|+|y|\\le 1}\\,\\,{e}^{x+y}\\,dA=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw a sketch of our region.\n\n![](images/4f/4f4e38950d36bf77ce4b2a907f07b3f9c4b40837729ef644f37ecfbd921aec8a.png)\n\n  \n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/b8/b8075ab5905ada88b2a198f73738b2c0c507371cfea32b560c02be4f0185c92f.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,-x-1\\le y\\le x+1\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,x-1\\le y\\le -x+1\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{|x|+|y|\\le 1}{e}^{x+y}\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}{e}^{x+y}\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}{e}^{x+y}\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{-x-1}^{x+1}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x-1}^{-x+1}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}[{e}^{x+y}]_{-x-1}^{x+1}\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{e}^{x+y}]_{x-1}^{-x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({e}^{2x+1}-{e}^{-1})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}(e-{e}^{2x-1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{e}^{2x+1}}{2}-{e}^{-1}x]}_{-1}^{0}+{[ex-\\frac{{e}^{2x-1}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[\\frac{e}{2}-(\\frac{{e}^{-1}}{2}+{e}^{-1})]+[(e-\\frac{e}{2})+\\frac{{e}^{-1}}{2}] \\\\  & =e-{e}^{-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323935 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129192 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa355fd-5d73-5cce-9c76-1edafae19751" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2685a435-3b0b-5556-928d-8890e89f39c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{51}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321449} {:answer/id #uuid "85db0642-7d1c-5c8d-a791-5339d42f6b66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{61}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322209} {:answer/id #uuid "c2d61461-1e0a-5e92-8afb-016303b4ade2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{81}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322658} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ee0989-2908-5bfb-9f66-c112c2783214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{71}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322689} {:answer/id #uuid "e9bcd73f-4f44-5e3e-887d-09a600ad1503" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{41}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6ee0989-2908-5bfb-9f66-c112c2783214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{71}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322689} :answer-field/id #uuid "07f87830-aaf6-5bb1-abec-9ce4771189f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1e162c6a-7b02-5223-a553-b91cdf5010fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-37767" :question/problem "![](images/8d/8de0dad0436135ef40aa26666d10659f4041275a915de153b6b4b45312c1c52f.png)\n\nEvaluate ${∬}_{D}{x}^{2}y\\,dA,$ where $D$ is the region shown in the picture above." :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into three type II regions ${D}_{1},$ ${D}_{2},$ and ${D}_{3},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/b5/b58fc3909d5be467999053336f67d41b88b43c984208c60f3d46ee8b7479df58.png)\n\nAs a result, we get \n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,-2\\le x\\le -1\\},\n$$\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,1\\le x\\le 2\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{3}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,-2\\le x\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{x}^{2}y\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}{x}^{2}y\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}{x}^{2}y\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{3}}{x}^{2}y\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{y\\text{ }\\,{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{-2}^{-1}\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{y\\text{ }\\,{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{3}{[\\frac{y\\text{ }\\,{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{-2}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{7y}{3}\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{7y}{3}\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{16y}{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{7}{3}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{16}{3}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}+\\frac{64}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{71}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475920 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129193 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "264eb5c1-fb55-5ed2-bc46-5548555bc98c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type I Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27c7f92a-5c64-5f2f-a12c-3e4b7e56d6f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{1-x}^{3-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475494} {:answer/id #uuid "8b2918b4-5b1a-5e09-96c3-37123de1ba55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{1-x}^{\\sqrt{3-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3-x}}^{\\sqrt{3-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475652} {:answer/id #uuid "8c2300f0-baa5-5212-b5f7-d261c57b46a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{1-x}^{\\sqrt{3-{x}^{2}}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3-x}}^{\\sqrt{3-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475654} {:answer/id #uuid "ddf08033-d820-539a-8135-8cad5b26ce10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{1-x}^{\\sqrt{3-{x}^{2}}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475781} {:answer/id #uuid "e9e13229-a93d-5417-8009-b20a01b65756" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{\\int }_{1-x}^{\\sqrt{3-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{x-3}^{3-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b2918b4-5b1a-5e09-96c3-37123de1ba55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{1-x}^{\\sqrt{3-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3-x}}^{\\sqrt{3-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475652} :answer-field/id #uuid "54e9c707-1747-52ad-abb8-366afb9bc3dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475858}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1f526958-5ff7-5f1e-b97a-1125f849ae32" :question/math-academy-id "q-82075" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $x=3-{y}^{2}$ and the line $y=1-x.$ \nExpress ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions." :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/8a/8a46756cd4842caf7977ef72ae05912a635843a06382b21136362455a94369e4.png)\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.   Notice that we're using that $x=3-{y}^{2}$ can be split into $y=\\pm \\sqrt{3-x}.$ \n\n![](images/43/43da7a61d7a4bff15274cdacbf1f3265c097edb8740583c69463460467f8100f.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,1-x\\le y\\le \\sqrt{3-x}\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 3,\\,-\\sqrt{3-x}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{3-x}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{1-x}^{\\sqrt{3-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3-x}}^{\\sqrt{3-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475969 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129194 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb3a9009-1c97-57c1-bc3c-45b318a62b8c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39f60118-786e-5b4f-b742-fa260616a9fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y/2}^{\\sqrt{2y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{(3y+2)/2}^{\\sqrt{2y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475522} {:answer/id #uuid "55af3ac3-2ce5-50b7-9a85-a4cefb08d592" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{2y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{(3y+2)/2}^{\\sqrt{2y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475567} {:answer/id #uuid "db123738-960e-56c7-b973-f03c45f9e841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y/2}^{\\sqrt{2y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(3y-2)/2}^{\\sqrt{2y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475774} {:answer/id #uuid "e161cf4c-90cd-5345-a9b9-1dfc2d9a1476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{\\sqrt{2y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(3y-2)/2}^{\\sqrt{2y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475788} {:answer/id #uuid "ee55bf76-b835-59b2-b361-2dd5c58bebd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}/2}^{2y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(2y+2)/3}^{\\sqrt{2y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db123738-960e-56c7-b973-f03c45f9e841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y/2}^{\\sqrt{2y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(3y-2)/2}^{\\sqrt{2y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475774} :answer-field/id #uuid "d14fe408-e710-5a6c-9dc2-c17893127e06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d88f3d27-3ac2-554c-ada9-11e1bf695d44" :question/math-academy-id "q-82116" :question/problem "![](images/7f/7fa5e4cd0c573ab5841e3ded221486ee2cabf6e00e1493c3de06fe4d9a87e3a7.png)\n\nConsider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $y=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2},$ $y=2x,$ and $y=\\frac{(2x+2)}{3},$ as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2} & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{2y} \\\\ y=2x & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{y}{2} \\\\ y=\\frac{2x+2}{3} & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{3y-2}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/63/63848a26cff0641ac83c73e809028852697212ce64a8cb954815d514922721a1.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{2y}\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\frac{3y-2}{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{2y}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y/2}^{\\sqrt{2y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(3y-2)/2}^{\\sqrt{2y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351394 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129194 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb3a9009-1c97-57c1-bc3c-45b318a62b8c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b79c9c9-fde7-5531-848c-1b193c278343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{\\int }_{1-y+e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1/2}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348545} {:answer/id #uuid "6b92393d-1a00-549f-b1c6-2066232ed66b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-y}^{{e}^{2}y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{2e}{\\int }_{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1+e-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349436} {:answer/id #uuid "a2810d7d-26d9-5b9f-a6da-a5a990de8ab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1-y}^{{e}^{y}}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy+{\\int }_{2}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{e-y}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349896} {:answer/id #uuid "faf384ee-a251-5a9f-a655-35c3a2e727fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1+e-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350658} {:answer/id #uuid "ff271755-5ab5-5878-ac9a-ac9de7768498" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{{e}^{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1+e-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff271755-5ab5-5878-ac9a-ac9de7768498" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{{e}^{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1+e-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350693} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7d1f385-1fe4-55c3-910c-932efd80aeb9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "96fc8cbf-3b1e-5dd2-9a47-105985216141" :question/math-academy-id "q-82135" :question/problem "![](images/41/4174f3930bb19223300539e1b4e9b7b191669aa4f701bff51e8349d0710ce6fb.png)\n\nConsider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curves $y={e}^{x},$ $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ and the lines $y=1+e-x$  and $y=1-x,$ as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y={e}^{x} & \\,⟹\\,x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y \\\\ y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,x={e}^{y} \\\\ y=1+e-x & \\,⟹\\,x=1+e-y \\\\ y=1-x & \\,⟹\\,x=1-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/4d/4df7cf2f33520a80270341d4a40b4a83d9f3c11ed8adb69fe1131a42bcd61d5a.png)\n\n    \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,1-y\\le x\\le {e}^{y}\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le e,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\le x\\le 1+e-y\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{{e}^{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1+e-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394366 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129194 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb3a9009-1c97-57c1-bc3c-45b318a62b8c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edf7f184-6600-513c-98a9-e621ee225359" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{4-2y}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{4-2y}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394368} {:answer/id #uuid "edc084ee-d037-55c9-8d5f-1af0f8274d8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(y-1)^{2}+2}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394369} {:answer/id #uuid "1512ad11-94d7-52a8-bd1c-4b27cbfbadbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{4-2y}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(y-1)^{2}+2}^{4-2y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394370} {:answer/id #uuid "9c2cd832-a593-5944-9882-b3d631c451c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{4-2y}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(y-1)^{2}+2}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394371} {:answer/id #uuid "5274f529-64a1-5518-ae40-8caee629efa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{(y-1)^{2}+2}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(y-1)^{2}+2}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c2cd832-a593-5944-9882-b3d631c451c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{4-2y}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(y-1)^{2}+2}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394371} :answer-field/id #uuid "04797421-9350-5d4c-9079-ec7a41aeb866" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394367}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9fc12f5e-e89a-5d92-929e-151cd796ef36" :question/math-academy-id "q-82358" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y=\\sqrt{x-2}+1,$ and the lines $y=2-\\frac{1}{2}x$ and $y=8-2x.$ Express ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=\\sqrt{x-2}+1 & \\,⟹\\,x=(y-1)^{2}+2 \\\\ y=2-\\frac{1}{2}x & \\,⟹\\,x=4-2y \\\\ y=8-2x & \\,⟹\\,x=4-\\frac{1}{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/3f/3f8e3ccfeac236d7fe9a502f599c61c404607a55ae809ec142019a3f881e1568.png)\n\n  \n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/31/3148cb0f499564db9cbfd6b635fef81dc47298789241af4a243c32dbf4dc8247.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,4-2y\\le x\\le 4-\\frac{1}{2}y\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,(y-1)^{2}+2\\le x\\le 4-\\frac{1}{2}y\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{4-2y}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(y-1)^{2}+2}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351418 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129192 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa355fd-5d73-5cce-9c76-1edafae19751" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f94319b-be48-578d-a42c-dad9428c9b5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349025} {:answer/id #uuid "578a6874-aefe-57e8-9cb3-47ff462bd36d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349251} {:answer/id #uuid "b6beafa1-1bd8-5f55-9eba-6b6e66490f45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350066} {:answer/id #uuid "c7237e65-b0d8-55a2-9393-52d10c49651b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350200} {:answer/id #uuid "e1c69c74-2f8c-5bfd-a3fb-3f4206368fd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7237e65-b0d8-55a2-9393-52d10c49651b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350200} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4b562c5-e9cf-59ac-9cdb-dd371b9f4a63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351048}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a00687a3-f424-5ed9-b2df-91dc74b795c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-82360" :question/problem "![](images/ad/ad8d4069ab0effd57ba58ccc4bf5792d5a014b114afb086e6d4b71d69ba14d2c.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is enclosed by the the curves $y={x}^{2}$ and $y=|x|,$ as shown in the picture. Evaluate ${∬}_{D}2x\\,dA.$" :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/2f/2fcb30778db2f051a7a819ae701808af59ac18d27c25a9c57ce678caa6c3ee3b.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le -x\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le x\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2x\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}2x\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}2x\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{-x}2x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x}2x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}2xy{|}_{{x}^{2}}^{-x}\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}2xy{|}_{{x}^{2}}^{x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}2x[-x-{x}^{2}]\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}2x[x-{x}^{2}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(-2{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3})\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}]}_{-1}^{0}+{[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =((0-(-\\frac{2}{3}(-1)^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}(-1)^{4}))+((\\frac{2}{3}(1)^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}(1)^{4})-0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351419 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129192 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa355fd-5d73-5cce-9c76-1edafae19751" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "118a2340-ee04-5e42-8b78-10f4638b24da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348600} {:answer/id #uuid "6749ded2-5b58-5631-9b85-8ecb08f12ff2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349394} {:answer/id #uuid "858a7d1d-a35e-5216-9b5a-1f3b7e4c84e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "77" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349667} {:answer/id #uuid "d3441c4c-6a81-5d07-9863-30030a1ac4f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350302} {:answer/id #uuid "eb7751d6-cf40-59f1-9635-6dfff3b8fcc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "858a7d1d-a35e-5216-9b5a-1f3b7e4c84e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "77" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349667} :answer-field/id #uuid "e929c9d6-0a89-5b39-8782-8590a74cb865" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351119}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "46c81894-7275-5b32-b94a-f373714d0ee2" :question/math-academy-id "q-82362" :question/problem "![](images/13/13275042f8b7b74e394b3cee1350c19cfa50ddf63899066682cbd0109f42d6bf.png)\n\nEvaluate ${∬}_{D}4xy\\,dA,$ where $D$ is the region shown in the picture above." :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/64/648121ff2a676f6a472a6e221dffe813eca55f914aed0ca9a285bb0d4cd81ab3.png)\n\n   \n\nAs a result, we get \n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\},\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}4xy\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}4xy\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}4xy\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}4xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[2x{y}^{2}]}_{1}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{[2x{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2x(9-1)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}2x(9-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}16x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}18x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8{x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{2}+9{x}^{2}{|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =8(4-0)+9(9-4) \\\\  & =77.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
